# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# GitHub Linguist language statistics
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# This is a Python-based market anomaly / fraud detection system with a
# Next.js dashboard. A large share of the TypeScript is *generated* UI
# scaffolding (shadcn/ui + Radix primitives), and the HTML/JS are generated
# documentation and tooling — none of which is hand-written application
# code. The rules below exclude them so the language bar reflects the real
# project. (Markdown is already excluded by Linguist as prose.)

# Generated UI primitives from shadcn/ui — not authored here
components/ui/**          linguist-vendored

# HTML documentation generated from Markdown by scripts/md-to-html.js
docs/PROJECT_DOCUMENTATION.html linguist-generated

# Documentation / build tooling, not part of the application
scripts/*.js             linguist-vendored

# Lockfiles (Linguist handles most, but be explicit)
package-lock.json        linguist-generated
